Subject: [PATCH] compose: drop the screen.left and screen.top lookup

The work area derivation reads no panel origin from the profile. The
profile schema has no screen.left or screen.top and forbids extra keys
under screen, so that lookup can only return its zero fallback.
screen.availLeft and screen.availTop come from the panel insets alone.
No value a page reads changes.

--- a/base/apostate/compose.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/compose.cc
@@ -1378,13 +1378,15 @@
 
   // availLeft/availTop are panel-relative: the Windows reference capture ran
   // on a second monitor at x=1920 and reported availLeft 1920 with a zero
-  // inset. So the inset is added to the panel origin, which is zero unless the
-  // panel states one.
-  const int origin_left = screen->FindInt("left").value_or(0);
-  const int origin_top = screen->FindInt("top").value_or(0);
-
-  screen->Set("avail_left", origin_left + *inset_left);
-  screen->Set("avail_top", origin_top + *inset_top);
+  // inset. So the inset is added to the panel origin, and the panel origin is
+  // always zero here because no profile can state one. This used to read
+  // "screen.left" and "screen.top" with a zero fallback, and
+  // config/profile.schema.json declares neither and forbids additional
+  // properties under screen, so both lookups could only ever miss. A profile
+  // with more than one display carries its origins per display in
+  // screen.displays[].left and .top, which this function does not touch.
+  screen->Set("avail_left", *inset_left);
+  screen->Set("avail_top", *inset_top);
   screen->Set("avail_width", *width - *inset_left - *inset_right);
   screen->Set("avail_height", *height - *inset_top - *inset_bottom);
 }
